cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Markov-K-means: stopping K-means on its unstable tail and finishing it by Markov chains of the centers and the labels"
abstract: >-
  Markov-K-means watches the state of a K-means run (how many points still change cluster,
  whether the centers travel or only jitter, whether the clusters reorganise or only swap
  members) and stops once only a few boundary points are still changing. It then finishes
  the run by Markov chains: the path of each center gives the position it is heading for or
  jittering around (a pseudo representative), every point is assigned to its nearest pseudo
  representative, and the points still undecided get soft memberships from their own label
  history (a point that keeps switching gets its share of time in each cluster).
  It works on exact Lloyd (Hamerly), 1/count mini-batch and constant-step (EMA) mini-batch
  K-means, and is a scikit-learn compatible estimator.
